From: Robert Sturla <rsturla@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] test/utils/ktesting: ensure minimum parallelism for TestParallel

TestParallel uses a 3-goroutine rendezvous barrier: each subtest calls
tCtx.Parallel(), signals wg.Done(), then blocks on wg.Wait(). All three
must run simultaneously for the barrier to resolve. The default
-test.parallel equals GOMAXPROCS, which can be < 3 in constrained build
environments, causing the third subtest to wait in waitParallel while
the other two are blocked on wg.Wait() — a deadlock.

Raise -test.parallel to at least 4 in TestMain when below threshold.

---
 test/utils/ktesting/main_test.go | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/test/utils/ktesting/main_test.go
+++ b/test/utils/ktesting/main_test.go
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ import (
 	"flag"
 	"fmt"
 	"os"
+	"strconv"
 	"testing"

 	"go.uber.org/goleak"
@@ -29,6 +30,15 @@ func TestMain(m *testing.M) {
 	// Bail out early when -help was given as parameter.
 	flag.Parse()

+	// TestParallel uses a 3-goroutine rendezvous barrier. The default
+	// -parallel value equals GOMAXPROCS, which may be < 3 in constrained
+	// build environments, causing a deadlock. Raise it to the minimum needed.
+	if p := flag.Lookup("test.parallel"); p != nil {
+		if n, _ := strconv.Atoi(p.Value.String()); n < 4 {
+			_ = p.Value.Set("4")
+		}
+	}
+
 	// Must be called *before* creating new goroutines.
 	goleakOpts := []goleak.Option{
 		goleak.IgnoreCurrent(),
